+### Public presence discloses its permanent spending half, 2026-10-14
+
+**Open; blocks the confidentiality premise of item 1.**
+`montana-node/tests/presence_disclosure_audit.rs` builds an actual node confirmation,
+accepts it through `verify_heavy`, then gives only its serialized proof to an observer.
+The observer reads the four lane words from a query. Every query contains the same words,
+and they equal the machine's permanent spending half. From those bytes the observer
+reproduces part and credit nullifiers at five heights, including earlier and later windows.
+A second machine is a negative control. This does not recover the original machine secret
+or a signing key, and no theft of value is claimed.
+
+The cause is exact: `presence::trace_of` fills each lane column with a constant, while
+`scheme::prove` interpolates the unmasked columns and publishes their evaluations. The
+interpolant of a constant is the same constant. Validity of the proof does not hide its
+witness. A change limited to standing's HMAC mask cannot repair this separate disclosure.
+
+The reproduction passed on the separate Linux verification host in 15.63 seconds, with
+the actual confirmation accepted first. The existing unauthorized-standing reproduction
+also passed: the same presence proof still accepts commitments to zero and `u64::MAX`.
+Both successes mean that the attacks reproduced. They are not acceptance evidence for
+a repaired window. The source archive contained 206 files, all checked before and after
+the runs. Its SHA-256 is
+`80b3a3ee8c2b483686ea1ee6be4025a40a90039d7c0cc5e36c7e15a3a9c3f9df`.
+
+The required relation remains in [WINDOW-STATEMENT.md](WINDOW-STATEMENT.md).
+Implementing an authenticated weight relation, a private fresh-sum proof, the canonical
+transition, ticket ownership and authenticated history remains necessary. A complete
+masking construction for the proof transcript is an additional prerequisite to calling
+those witnesses hidden. No production verifier or protocol parameter was changed by
+this reproduction, and item 1 remains open.
