+#### The arithmetic step of the window accumulation
+
+The arithmetic step is a component of the complete window statement of Consensus. Its verifier
+establishes one modular multiply-add per coefficient and binds its challenges. Authentication of
+the predecessor, the committed population and weights, the transition and the runner's ticket
+belongs to the complete statement. Acceptance of this component establishes none of those
+additional assertions.
+
+The component's public input is the incoming accumulators in repetition order, the one instance,
+the outgoing accumulators in repetition order, and the challenges in repetition order. Each
+commitment has the coefficients of the standing commitment laid polynomial by polynomial; each
+coefficient and challenge is an unsigned four-byte little-endian integer. The repetition count
+is the count in Consensus. Every coefficient is strictly below the commitment modulus. A length
+differing from that exact layout, including an extra suffix, is refused.
+
+Let `prefix` be exactly the incoming accumulators followed by the instance. Both are fixed before
+the challenges are drawn. Here `commitment_modulus` denotes `q` in "The commitment that carries
+standing", and `window_air_hash` is the window description's identifier in "The arithmetization,
+and how the set is bound to it". With `S` and the canonical words of a digest as defined above:
+
+```
+step_transcript = S(window_air_hash || prefix)
+digest_i        = S(step_transcript || i_8B_LE), i from zero
+limit           = proof_field - (proof_field mod commitment_modulus)
+```
+
+Read the four canonical words of each digest in order. Discard a word at or above `limit`;
+otherwise take its remainder modulo `commitment_modulus`, discarding a zero remainder. Continue
+until every repetition has its challenge. The counter never wraps. The complete buckets below
+`limit` give each remainder the same number of preimages, so rejection of zero gives a uniform
+draw over the nonzero scalars under the transcript's random-oracle model. A verifier repeats this
+derivation; challenges supplied in the component's public input must match exactly. The outgoing
+accumulators are bound by the proof transcript and do not enter the earlier challenge derivation.
+
+The arithmetic description also holds a multiplicative inverse of the challenge in `proof_field`
+at every active coefficient row. Their product equals one there and zero on idle rows. Thus a
+zero challenge fails the arithmetic constraints themselves. This constraint and the native
+derivation are distinct obligations: the former excludes zero and the latter excludes a
+claimant-chosen nonzero challenge.
+
+**Invariants of the arithmetic step:**
+
+- Its input has exactly the layout above, and every coefficient has its canonical encoding.
+- Its incoming accumulators and instance determine its challenges before its outputs are formed.
+- Every active challenge is nonzero, both in the description and in the verifying algorithm.
+- The verifying algorithm recomputes every challenge and verifies the proof under the current
+  arithmetic description; a retired description is a different statement.
+- Its result is an arithmetic relation. Only the complete window verifier may establish finality
